{"id":"beelzebub","name":"Beelzebub","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:beelzebub"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Beelzebub","text":"(Gr. form Beel’zebul), the name given to Satan, and found only in the New Testament (Matt. 10:25; 12:24, 27; Mark 3:22). It is probably the same as Baalzebub (q.v.), the god of Ekron, meaning “the lord of flies,” or, as others think, “the lord of dung,” or “the dung-god.”"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G954","lemma":"Βεελζεβούλ","xlit":"Beelzeboúl","gloss":"dung-god","kjv":"Beelzebub","count":7,"share":0.88},{"strong":"G1140","lemma":"δαιμόνιον","xlit":"daimónion","gloss":"a dæmonic being","kjv":"devil, god","count":6,"share":0.75},{"strong":"G1544","lemma":"ἐκβάλλω","xlit":"ekbállō","gloss":"to eject","kjv":"bring forth, cast, drive, expel","count":6,"share":0.75},{"strong":"G758","lemma":"ἄρχων","xlit":"árchōn","gloss":"a first","kjv":"chief, magistrate, prince, ruler","count":3,"share":0.38},{"strong":"G2923","lemma":"κριτής","xlit":"kritḗs","gloss":"a judge","kjv":"judge","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"G2071","lemma":"ἔσομαι","xlit":"ésomai","gloss":"will be","kjv":"shall  be, come, X may have, X fall","count":2,"share":0.25}],"verses":["Matt.10.25","Matt.12.24","Matt.12.27","Mark.3.22","Luke.11.15","Luke.11.18","Luke.11.19","2Kgs.1.2"],"related":[{"id":"baal-zebub","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"scoffing","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.036,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"satan","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.027,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"demons","type":"lexical","strong":"G1140","why":"both lead with δαιμόνιον (G1140)"},{"id":"epicureans","type":"lexical","strong":"G1140","why":"both lead with δαιμόνιον (G1140)"}],"works":[{"work":"anf04","title":"Ante-Nicene Fathers, Volume 4: Tertullian (Part Fourth), Minucius Felix, Commodian, Origen (Parts First and Second)","count":1,"chapters":[{"chap